From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: retain the tethered warm boot state

A tethered kernel inherits initialized hardware rather than power-on
state. Retain the board-selected warm handoff state so probe and
shutdown do not discard resources needed by the incoming kernel.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800-0-3.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800-0-3.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800-0-3.dtsi
index 3277a73bb..f6449a7e6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800-0-3.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800-0-3.dtsi
@@ -443,3 +443,7 @@ pmu {
  * the S8003 (APL1022) on 16nm. There are some minor differences
  * such as timing in cpufreq state transistions.
  */
+
+/ {
+	apple,reserve-pstore;
+};
